---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'Nether Coordinate Calculator',
    url: 'https://minepedia.app/tools/nether-calculator/',
    applicationCategory: 'GameApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' }
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How do nether portal coordinates work?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'One block traveled in the Nether equals eight blocks in the Overworld on the X and Z axes. Divide Overworld X and Z by 8 to get the matching Nether position; multiply Nether X and Z by 8 for the Overworld. Y stays the same.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Why did my portal link to the wrong place?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Portals search for an existing portal near the scaled coordinates. If two Overworld portals are within 1024 blocks (128 in the Nether), they can link to the same Nether portal. Build your Nether-side portal at the exact converted coordinates to force correct linking.' } }
    ]
  }
];
---
<Base title="Nether Coordinate Calculator" description="Convert Minecraft coordinates between the Overworld and the Nether (8:1 ratio). Find exactly where to build your linked portal. Java and Bedrock." canonicalPath="/tools/nether-calculator/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/tools/">Tools</a> / Nether Calculator</nav>
    <h1>Nether Coordinate Calculator</h1>
    <p class="sub">One Nether block = eight Overworld blocks. Convert instantly and build your portals in the right spot.</p>
    <div class="quick-answer"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Overworld to Nether: divide X and Z by 8. Nether to Overworld: multiply X and Z by 8. Y never changes.</div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:16px;margin:24px 0">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Overworld to Nether</h3>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin:12px 0">
          <input id="ow-x" type="number" placeholder="X" class="search-input" style="padding:10px" />
          <input id="ow-y" type="number" placeholder="Y" class="search-input" style="padding:10px" />
          <input id="ow-z" type="number" placeholder="Z" class="search-input" style="padding:10px" />
        </div>
        <button class="copy-btn" id="ow-btn" style="padding:10px 20px">Convert to Nether</button>
        <p id="ow-out" style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent-bright)"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Nether to Overworld</h3>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin:12px 0">
          <input id="n-x" type="number" placeholder="X" class="search-input" style="padding:10px" />
          <input id="n-y" type="number" placeholder="Y" class="search-input" style="padding:10px" />
          <input id="n-z" type="number" placeholder="Z" class="search-input" style="padding:10px" />
        </div>
        <button class="copy-btn" id="n-btn" style="padding:10px 20px">Convert to Overworld</button>
        <p id="n-out" style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent-bright)"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2>How portal linking works</h2>
    <p>Minecraft scales horizontal coordinates 8:1 between dimensions. When you enter a portal, the game converts your position (X/8, Z/8 going to the Nether) and looks for an active portal nearby: within 128 blocks in the Nether, 1024 in the Overworld (Java). If none exists, it creates one.</p>
    <h2>Fix a broken portal link</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Take your Overworld portal's X and Z and divide by 8 (round to whole numbers).</li>
      <li>In the Nether, break the wrongly linked portal and build a new one at exactly those coordinates.</li>
      <li>Re-light it and re-enter from the Overworld side. The link is now 1:1.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Related: <a href="/guides/how-to-make-nether-portal/">How to Make a Nether Portal</a></p>
  </div>
  <script>
    function conv(ids, out, fn) {
      const [x, y, z] = ids.map(id => parseFloat((document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement).value));
      const el = document.getElementById(out)!;
      if (isNaN(x) || isNaN(z)) { el.textContent = 'Enter at least X and Z.'; return; }
      const yy = isNaN(y) ? 64 : y;
      el.textContent = `X: ${fn(x)}, Y: ${yy}, Z: ${fn(z)}`;
    }
    document.getElementById('ow-btn')!.addEventListener('click', () => conv(['ow-x','ow-y','ow-z'], 'ow-out', v => Math.round(v / 8)));
    document.getElementById('n-btn')!.addEventListener('click', () => conv(['n-x','n-y','n-z'], 'n-out', v => Math.round(v * 8)));
  </script>
</Base>
